{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790346889,"nonce":"mRRCqG47tCTNY3shRg1p4VenT4I=","title":"Generic functions compile once with T as an opaque word; calls never instantiate them","message":"monomorphize_module (crates/compiler/src/monomorphize.rs) instantiates only calls that carry explicit type_args. ZynML builds every TypedCall with `type_args: vec![]` (crates/zyn_peg/src/runtime2/interpreter.rs, TypedCall construction), so a generic function is compiled once with T left opaque, and a generic whose body branches on or prints a T value shows `\u003copaque type_id=...\u003e`. Type arguments should be inferred at the call by unifying parameter types with argument types, then passed to monomorphization.","files":null}]}